            "evidence": [
              "Reviewed all 14 manifest paths from a security/risk lens.",
              "CI change replaces `go run staticcheck@v0.7.0` with a build from tools/lint, whose go.sum pins checksums for every module; this reduces supply-chain risk (go build verifies against go.sum, fails on mismatch or missing entry). No secrets, new network endpoints, or elevated permissions are added in .github/workflows/ci.yml.",
              "Workflow shell uses only $GITHUB_WORKSPACE and $RUNNER_TEMP, which are runner-controlled and not attacker-influenced; no untrusted github.event context is interpolated into run scripts.",
              "tools/lint/go.mod and go.sum list honnef.co/go/tools v0.7.0 and its dependencies with h1 hashes; no known-vulnerable dependency evidence is visible in the patch. deadcode remains pinned via go run @v0.48.0, which is unchanged pre-existing behavior.",
              "Telemetry changes add a NoID counter and refactor to named constants and a keepMode type; calls without an ID were previously dropped as skipped and are now counted separately, with no new data exposure (tests assert no_id never reaches stdout) and no new input-handling surface.",
              "Test-only changes in tui/backend_tag_test.go and tools/deterministic-check-runner/main_test.go adapt guards to the new CI spelling; they do not affect production behavior."
            ]
          }
        }
