            "lens": "review-reliability",
            "findings": [],
            "evidence": [
              "telemetry/readers.go: parse now returns true for a call line with no ID, and readFile counts it as NoID without calling keep. Such lines are therefore never treated as duplicates and are no longer counted as Skipped. This is the requested R3-001 change. telemetry/readers_test.go (TestNoIDCounted) and telemetry/cmd/telemetry/main_test.go (TestStatsNoID) assert the exact Stats and stderr values for both Claude and Pi, and that no_id does not reach stdout.",
              "telemetry/cmd/telemetry/main.go: the keepMode refactor keeps the old behavior. keepTop sorts, cuts and prints the note as before, and keepLatest keeps the last N rows with no note. TestTopLatestDays covers N between 1 and the number of days, which was the requested gap.",
              "telemetry/aggregate.go: the named index constants use keyed array literals for both keys and outputs, so each dimension is paired with its slice by name. The array size is the `dimensions` constant, which makes a mismatch a compile-time error.",
              "tools/deterministic-check-runner/main_test.go: staticcheckRequirePattern matches only a `honnef.co/go/tools vX` requirement line. It does not match the `tool honnef.co/go/tools/cmd/staticcheck` line. The test fails if ci.yml re-pins staticcheck with `@`, and it fails if the go.mod requirement is missing.",
              "tui/backend_tag_test.go: testFileReader now recognizes the staticcheck binary invocation and classifies the `go build` line that produces it as reading no test files. The table test covers both lines.",
              ".github/workflows/ci.yml: all six jobs build staticcheck from tools/lint, where go.sum pins it. I found no reliability regression visible in the diff. Whether the go 1.21 jobs switch toolchain through GOTOOLCHAIN=auto depends on workflow setup that this diff does not show. The candidate's notes record that this was verified."
            ]
          }
        }
